  "sourceConclusions": [
    "All seven ID-bearing row kinds are validated for duplicate primary keys before any lookup or reconciliation output is constructed; export rows have no id field in this snapshot contract.",
    "Duplicate IDs with conflicting organizations/agents are rejected identically in either order, with only a fixed row-kind code; equal IDs in separate kinds remain valid.",
    "Exception explicit workday, event workday, and evidence-subject workday must agree, including evidence attached to either event or site transition and references belonging to the same employee.",
    "Mismatch produces one finite EXCEPTION_SUBJECT_SCOPE_MISMATCH for the affected exception; coherent same-workday combinations remain accepted.",
    "Frozen snapshots, including duplicate and cross-workday inputs, remain unchanged. Successful and mismatch outputs contain counts/codes and repair NONE without row or cursor identifiers.",
    "Unchanged job calls reconciliation before commitCursor; duplicate exceptions reject and mismatches return before cursor advancement or subsequent page load.",
    "Changes do not introduce a database adapter, scheduler, lease activation, production effects or changes to shared cursor/lease helpers."
  ],
